It was basically a rhetorical ploy to have postponed giving an instance of a cognitive architecture until now. Many instances of cognitive architecture exist, including connectionist architectures.15 Newell was very committed to an architecture called Soar, which has continued to evolve and grow since his death (Newell, 1990; for current developments in Soar, see sitemaker.umich.edu/soar).
